%S A401304 2,3,2,2,41,3,3,41,17,5,179,263,79,179,47,17,71,83,11,79,653,2,1321,
%T A401304 79,11,167,83,3,71,31,2393,719,89,2,107,479,397,503,5,379,337,151,607,
%U A401304 233,17,139,2,37,839,743,4903,311,2861,1013,211,379,5,1213,19,151
%N A401304 a(n) is the least prime p such that (p^m + q^m)/(p+q) is also prime where m=prime(n), where q is the next prime after p, or -1 if no such p exists.
%e A401304 Let m = prime(2) = 3. For p = 2 the next prime is q = 3, and (2^3 + 3^3)/(2 + 3) = 35/5 = 7, a prime. Since p = 2 is the smallest prime for which (p^m + q^m)/(p + q) is prime, it follows that a(2) = 2.
%e A401304 Let m = prime(3) = 5. For p = 3 the next prime is q = 5, and (3^5 + 5^5)/(3 + 5) = 3368/8 = 421, a prime. Since p = 3 is the smallest prime for which (p^m + q^m)/(p + q) is prime, it follows that a(3) = 3.
%e A401304 Let m = prime(4) = 7. For p = 2 the next prime is q = 3, and (2^7 + 3^7)/(2 + 3) = 2315/5 = 463, a prime. Since p = 2 is the smallest prime for which (p^m + q^m)/(p + q) is prime, it follows that a(4) = 2.
%o A401304 (PARI) a(n) = my(m=prime(n)); forprime(p=2, oo, my(q=nextprime(p+1)); if(ispseudoprime((p^m+q^m)/(p+q)), return(p))); \\ _Alper Ferudun_, Oct 20 2026
